{# Physical Letters: an NPC writes a letter to someone the cheap pass proposed
   (physical_letters_npc_propose); this call judges whether and why.  Sent with
   PublicSendCustomPromptToLLM; context:
     npc             UUID, name of the writer
     place           where the writer lives
     recipient       UUID, name, place
     player          the player's name
     memories        the writer's newest memories (letters excluded)
     correspondence  their earlier letters to each other that the writer knows of, oldest
                     first: from, to, days_ago, body #}

{% set actor = decnpc(npc.UUID) %}
[ system ]
    You are writing a letter as {{ actor.name }}, in {{ place }}, to {{ recipient.name }} in {{ recipient.place }}. Stay true to {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} personality, background and speech.

    {{ render_character_profile("full", npc.UUID) }}

    ## {{ recipient.name }}
    {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", recipient.UUID) }}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    {% if memories and length(memories) > 0 %}
    ## What {{ actor.name }} Has Been Through Lately
    {% for memory in memories -%}
    - {{ memory }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if correspondence and length(correspondence) > 0 %}
    ## Their Earlier Letters
    {% for earlier in correspondence %}
    From {{ earlier.from }} to {{ earlier.to }}, {% if earlier.days_ago == 0 %}earlier today{% else if earlier.days_ago == 1 %}a day ago{% else %}{{ earlier.days_ago }} days ago{% endif %}:
    ```
    {{ earlier.body }}
    ```
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    First decide what ties {{ actor.name }} to {{ recipient.name }}, from the profiles, the memories and Skyrim's lore, and what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} would write to them about now. Don't invent a closeness they don't have: a shared trade or hold can be a reason for a letter of that kind. If there's no real tie or reason, don't write.

    Otherwise write the letter, a few short paragraphs at most, signed with {{ actor.possessiveAdjective }} name, in a tone that matches the tie. News of what {{ actor.subjectivePronoun }} has lived through, {{ player }} included, is fine if it matters to {{ recipient.name }}.

    Return JSON only:
    - 'tie': how they're connected, in a few words
    - 'purpose': what the letter is for, in a few words
    - 'write': true, or false if {{ actor.name }} doesn't write
    - 'letter': the letter, or ""
    - 'memory': one or two first-person sentences {{ actor.name }} keeps of writing it, or ""
    - 'emotion': one word
    - 'importance': 0.0-1.0
[ end user ]
